course: dictionary
lesson: 7336
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it, which is its context. The word plantain can mean a fruit or a plant.
explain: Look for clues. «Fried plantain» is a food, so the fruit is meant: a big banana-like fruit, usually cooked before eating. «Firing plantain heads like little guns» is something you do outdoors, so the plant is meant: a common wild plant with flat leaves close to the ground.
explain: Phrases help too. «Ripe plantain» and «green plantain» are about the fruit, while «ribwort plantain» names a wild plant. When a word has two meanings, try each one in the sentence and see which one fits.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning.
fact: «Plantain» can mean a fruit like a big banana, usually cooked before eating.
fact: Plantain fruit is popular in Africa, the Caribbean and Latin America, and is often fried, boiled or baked.
fact: «Plantain» can also mean a common wild plant, or weed, with flat leaves close to the ground and thin spikes of tiny flowers.
fact: Ribwort plantain grows on lawns and paths, and its stems can be looped to flick their heads like little guns.
exercise: «Fried plantain is a favourite side dish in the Caribbean.» What is a plantain here? | A wild plant with flat leaves on a lawn | *A fruit like a big banana, cooked before eating | A kind of flower with a dandelion clock
exercise: «Children fire plantain heads like little guns on the school field.» What does plantain mean here? | A type of bread | *A common wild plant with thin spikes of tiny flowers | A green fruit to be fried | A dandelion clock
exercise: Which phrase names the wild plant, not the fruit? | *ribwort plantain | ripe plantain | green plantain | fried plantain
test: Mia says plantain is always a banana. What is wrong with her idea? | It is only a name for a cooked dish | It is a kind of flower only | *It can also mean a common wild plant with flat leaves | She is right, plantain is always a banana
test: In «Ribwort plantain stems can be looped to flick their heads», what does plantain mean? | *A wild plant | A type of banana | A fruit that is fried | A kind of cake
exam: Which clue in «Fried plantain is a favourite side dish» best shows that plantain is a food? | green | *fried | wild | sweet
